# Responsive Lesson Layout

All lesson markup must work from 320px phones to desktop without horizontal page scroll.

## Required patterns

- `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">` on every page.
- Use CSS classes from `src/styles/lesson.css` and design tokens from `tokens.css`.
- Grids must collapse: multi-column → single column on small screens (see `.warm-grid`, `.task-grid`).
- Wide tables: wrap in `.vocab-table-wrap` for horizontal scroll inside the container only.
- Typography: use `clamp()` for headings; never fixed pixel font sizes for body text.
- Touch targets: interactive elements (future) min 44×44px; adequate padding on cards.
- No fixed heights on content blocks — let content flow naturally.

## Forbidden

- Fixed canvas sizes (e.g. 3508px width) for web lessons.
- Absolute positioning for main content layout.
- Hiding essential content on mobile.

## Breakpoint reference

- 480px — 2-column match/ru-cues grids
- 640px — warm-up 2-col, phrase grid 2-col
- 768px — lesson header 2-col
- 900px — speaking zone 2-col
- 1024px — task grid 3-col, vocab zone 2-col

Test mentally at 320px, 768px, and 1280px before finishing.
